WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.033
-Our next guest is a talented drag performer and singer

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.434
who has won both "RuPaul's Drag Race"

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.100
and "RuPaul's Drag Race All Stars."

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.467
She stars as Mama Morton in the Tony-winning revival

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.667
of "Chicago" on Broadway at the Ambassador Theatre.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:15.901
Please welcome to the show Jinkx Monsoon!

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:17.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:25.901
♪♪

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:34.200
♪♪

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.801
Jinkx, we are so happy to have you in New York City.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.534
-Thank you. I'm having a great time.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.667
-It feels like you belong in New York City,

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.601
but you, of course, are from Portland, Oregon.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:46.501
How are you enjoying your time in this fair city?

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:48.934
-I'm enjoying it a lot because I'm staying in Brooklyn.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:50.801
-Okay. [ Laughter ]

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.601
You're working, of course, in Broadway.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.200
Does that mean you're not spending

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.501
a lot of time in Times Square?

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:58.734
-Normally I like to stay walking distance

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.000
from the theater because things can go wrong.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.167
-Of course. -And --

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.868
But when walking distance from the theater

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:08.334
means living in Times Square, then we forego that rule.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.701
[ Laughter ] -Okay.

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:11.501
So you're willing to take a subway.

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.968
-Well, imagine this trying to bob and weave

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.567
through the people on Times Square.

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.033
-Yeah, there are.

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:20.267
-If I had a staff and I could separate the people, you know,

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.367
like Moses. -You deserve that.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.000
-Yeah. -You deserve a Moses staff.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.033
-Come on! [ Laughs ]

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:29.133
-So, this is very exciting. You are doing the show.

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:30.434
You're playing Mama Morton.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:33.133
And this is a role you loved and a show you loved.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.167
-Yes. -Which was incredibly helpful

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:36.968
because you only had a week of rehearsals.

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.734
-I know, and they don't tell you --

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:41.834
when your dreams come true, it moves really quickly.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.000
-Uh-huh. -[ Laughs ]

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.667
But, you know, "Chicago" is pretty much

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.167
why I started doing drag.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:52.133
'Cause I was 15 years old. I was a "boy." And, um...

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:54.901
And I saw the movie "Chicago," and I was like,

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.934
"Well, those are the roles I should be playing.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.234
I guess I have to start dressing up like a woman now."

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:01.734
And it was pretty much, you know, like two weeks later,

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:05.267
I was a full-fledged drag queen, which -- in Portland

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.634
you can be a 15-year-old drag queen. Did you know that?

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:10.767
-No, I did not know that. That's incredible.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.200
What a wonderful feature to have for your fair city.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.567
-Yeah. It's a good place.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.033
-You have -- Speaking of a good place,

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.634
you've got a good place in --

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.334
This is some interior shots of your home in Portland.

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:23.467
And let me just say it is -- I would expect nothing less

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.200
than the design of your beautiful --

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.133
-Yes. It's a beautiful chaos. -Yeah, beautiful chaos.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:29.801
You have room for lodgers, right?

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.300
You have people who -- -Yeah.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.234
You know, we were doing Airbnb for a while.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:36.567
You could stay at "Monsoon Manor."

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:39.501
Then, I don't know if you know, but there was a pandemic.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:41.601
-Mm-hmm. -And that changed things.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:44.334
So now I have long-term renters, and they all happen to be,

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:47.267
like, my chosen family members who I've known most of my life.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:50.601
So it's very much -- It's -- I don't know.

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:53.400
It has all the makings of being a sitcom,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.868
like, if "Friends" were just all gay people.

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:57.000
-Okay. -Yeah.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.367 --> 00:03:00.467
-I think people would watch that.

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:02.667
-I think that's what "Drag Race" is, actually.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.934
-Yeah. Speaking of "Drag Race."

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:07.000
You know, I'm not a super fan of the show,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.234
but I am aware of the fact

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:10.434
that you have won two different seasons.

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:11.634
-Yes.

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:13.033
-You have not given yourself this title.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:15.400
It has been bestowed upon you. "Queen of All Queens."

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.734
How does that -- [Cheers and applause]

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:21.334
-[ Laughs ] It's --

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:24.801
It feels funny because there are so many drag queens.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:28.701
And to say one queen is the "Queen of All Queens"

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.868
is like trying to say an apple is queen of all oranges.

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.200
You know?

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.267
But you can't really disagree with RuPaul

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.100
'cause she's the Grand High Witch.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.033
-Yeah, exactly. -You know?

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.334
So I'm taking it. I'm owning it.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.033
-Yeah, you've got to. Did you --

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:46.334
Was the second win as exciting as the first win?

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:48.000
-Probably much more exciting.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.133
Have you ever done something once every 10 years?

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:52.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.000
You have a lot of time

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.501
to build up anticipation between two things.

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:58.334
-Yeah. -Um, Seth, may I ask?

00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.067
-Yeah. -Are you straight?

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:01.367
-Yeah. -You sure?

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.968
-Yeah. -Okay.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:04.167
Let me double check.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.834
You can understand what I'm saying when I...

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:07.033
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:10.200
-Okay so, "Drag Race" is like the Super Bowl

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.033
if there were eight teams and each team was only one person

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:15.667
and they also had to make dresses.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:18.667
-Okay. I think I fully follow now.

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.200
Thank you so much.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.434
You spoke with your family,

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:25.767
and your family all came to see "Chicago."

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:28.334
Do you get a little extra nervous when you have family --

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.167
-No. I get nervous --

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:32.701
I want to make sure they're going to behave themselves.

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:34.801
-Oh, do you have that kind of family?

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:37.467
-It was like the Beverly Hillbillies do Broadway.

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.934
-Okay. -No.

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.634
It was really, really wonderful.

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:44.400
My mom hasn't made such a big trip in years.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.033
And my best friend, who is also my business partner, did it --

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:50.501
set up everything for my family,

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:53.534
so no one even texted me even once,

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.367
which was a dream come true.

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:58.334
-I would love -- If I could have your friend

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:02.434
fill in for me, just for a week, would be wonderful.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:04.400
-Yeah, yeah. They're a good buffer.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.567
But my straight brother,

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:10.934
the only straight brother I have,

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:13.367
it was his birthday on opening night.

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:15.300
And he's also a middle child.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.000
So I was so prepared for him to be like,

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.167
[Dull voice] "Oh, you couldn't have your opening night

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:21.067
on some other night?" -Right.

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.000
That's a very good straight guy, by the way.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.234
-Thank you, thank you.

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:27.100
-I heard a little of myself in that.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.667
Pretty much how I talk on my birthday.

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:31.300
I'm like, "I can't believe we got to do that on my birthday."

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.601
-But instead, he said, "You mean I get to spend

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:36.701
my birthday watching you make your Broadway debut?"

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.000
-That's pretty cool.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.501
-They came out the stage door with me.

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:41.367
There were a lot of fans waiting, and I made them

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:44.234
all sing "Happy Birthday" to Jeremy.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.234
And then I held him as he cried like a baby.

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:49.067
-Oh, well, there you go! That's a good birthday!

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:51.567
[ Applause ] Now, can you tell --

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.801
Obviously I imagine you can tell out the stage door,

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.434
but can you tell when the show starts --

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:57.901
are there drag-queen fans in the audience?

00:05:57.901 --> 00:06:00.467
-Well, especially opening night, I have to say,

00:06:00.467 --> 00:06:04.467
I am so proud of the LGBTQ+ community for opening night

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.968
because the energy was palpable.

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:11.167
And as we were getting closer and closer to my first entrance,

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:14.234
you could feel kind of like a rumbling building.

00:06:14.234 --> 00:06:16.934
And there was just uncontainable excitement.

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:19.968
But even though they may have been there to celebrate me

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:21.968
that night, they also celebrated

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:24.167
every single performer, every single number.

00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:26.167
It was the most generous audience.

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:27.934
And I was like, "Look at us showing up

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:30.834
at Broadway like this." You know?

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:32.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:34.133
-And you, yourself -- you talk about

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:35.601
that rumble in the crowd.

00:06:35.601 --> 00:06:37.267
How are you at --

00:06:37.267 --> 00:06:39.334
Do you get butterflies on that opening night?

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:41.501
Are you good at containing it? Are you good at --

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:44.067
-I am pretty good. I've been doing it for 20 years.

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:46.300
-There you go. Yeah.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.834
-So I'm pretty good at, like, knowing what to expect.

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:51.834
But, really, what has made this experience so wonderful

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:55.133
is that I was able to rehearse a show in nine days

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:57.067
because the team is so fantastic.

00:06:57.067 --> 00:06:59.300
They treated me like I've been doing this role for years.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.601
They treated me like family.

00:07:01.601 --> 00:07:03.133
And the performers.

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:08.100
Charlotte d'Amboise as Roxie. Brilliant.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.767
Lana Gordon as Velma.

00:07:09.767 --> 00:07:11.734
Her and I have most our scenes together.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:16.400
We're electric together. I dare -- I do say so myself.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.701
And then James T. Lane was taking over Billy

00:07:19.701 --> 00:07:21.801
at the same time I was taking over Mama.

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:24.000
So I wasn't the only newbie to the cast.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.601
And it was just -- It's just like a family.

00:07:27.601 --> 00:07:29.033
And I wasn't expecting that.

00:07:29.033 --> 00:07:30.901
I thought it was going to be work, work, work, work, work.

00:07:30.901 --> 00:07:33.467
Instead, it's been like a party. -Well, that's wonderful.

00:07:33.467 --> 00:07:35.200
I'm so happy to hear it's going so well.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.501
And I apologize now. I am going to put you on the spot.

00:07:37.501 --> 00:07:39.968
Because I know you are a wonderful impressionist,

00:07:39.968 --> 00:07:42.000
and I've got three I would like to ask you to do.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.167
-Sure, sure, sure.

00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:45.167
-Could you do a little Judy Garland for us?

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:46.801
-[As Judy Garland] Oh, Seb. Seb.

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:50.200
I'm so happy to be here, Seb.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.901
Seb, I love your show.

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:54.968
Are you familiar with Johnny Carson?

00:07:54.968 --> 00:07:56.434
-Yes, of course.

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:59.000
-I did the Carson show a few -- I think.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.334
I'm sure I probably did.

00:08:01.334 --> 00:08:02.834
-Very good.

00:08:02.834 --> 00:08:04.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:05.734
This is a little trickier.

00:08:05.734 --> 00:08:07.133
This is a friend of mine this time.

00:08:07.133 --> 00:08:08.634
This is Natasha Lyonne.

00:08:08.634 --> 00:08:09.901
Can you do -- -Yeah.

00:08:09.901 --> 00:08:12.467
[As Natasha Lyonne] Ah, Seth! Oh, my God! Seth!

00:08:12.467 --> 00:08:15.767
Seth, I-I woke up late.

00:08:15.767 --> 00:08:17.901
I took a little washy showy.

00:08:17.901 --> 00:08:21.100
Oh, New York, right? Seth, you know New York.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.734
Oh, my God!

00:08:22.734 --> 00:08:24.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.400
-Very -- Nailed both the voice and the physicality.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.834
-[Normal voice] And the mannerisms, thank you.

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:30.868
-Alright, now -- This one's a little tough for me.

00:08:30.868 --> 00:08:32.934
'Cause I do an excellent Jennifer Coolidge, as well.

00:08:32.934 --> 00:08:34.701
-You want to do dueling Jennifer Coolidges?

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:36.734
-Yeah, I'm a little worried, because I will say --

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:38.767
I know for a fact yours is worlds bett--

00:08:38.767 --> 00:08:40.033
-[As Jennifer Coolidge] Wow, wow.

00:08:40.033 --> 00:08:42.234
-[As Jennifer Coolidge] Wow.

00:08:42.234 --> 00:08:43.367
What are you doing here?

00:08:43.367 --> 00:08:45.667
-You know something, Seth?

00:08:45.667 --> 00:08:48.968
The gays just love me!

00:08:48.968 --> 00:08:51.934
And, uh, thanks to the gays, the three of us have been

00:08:51.934 --> 00:08:56.934
in show business for 40 years and goin' strong!

00:08:56.934 --> 00:08:58.033
Yeah!

00:08:58.033 --> 00:09:02.868
-Yeah. I'm so -- Wow!

00:09:02.868 --> 00:09:04.601
Wow. It's like looking in a mirror.

00:09:04.601 --> 00:09:06.601
-[Normal voice] Are you sure that's not Owen Wilson?

00:09:06.601 --> 00:09:07.834
-[Normal voice] It is Owen Wilson.

00:09:07.834 --> 00:09:10.901
-That's Owen Wilson, yeah. -But I think the --

00:09:10.901 --> 00:09:12.834
How dare you!

00:09:12.834 --> 00:09:14.934
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.934 --> 00:09:17.834
See, so, like, Owen Wilson is to Jennifer Coolidge

00:09:17.834 --> 00:09:20.901
what the Super Bowl is to "Drag Race."

00:09:20.901 --> 00:09:22.567
-"Drag Race." Yes, exactly.

00:09:22.567 --> 00:09:23.801
You're really starting

00:09:23.801 --> 00:09:25.267
to put things together all on your own.

00:09:25.267 --> 00:09:26.968
-It's all a puzzle piece. You know what I mean?

00:09:26.968 --> 00:09:28.734
-Would you do me a favor? -Yeah, what do you need?

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:32.100
-Would you tell your brother Josh I've had a crush on him

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.934
since I was a teenager?

00:09:33.934 --> 00:09:36.334
-Really. Well, hello, Jinkx!

00:09:36.334 --> 00:09:38.400
-Well, I'm s-- I mean, you're very attractive.

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.834
-Well, nice save.

00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:41.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.334 --> 00:09:44.434
-But I was a young person watching Josh on "Mad TV."

00:09:44.434 --> 00:09:46.634
-Yeah. -And "That '70s Show."

00:09:46.634 --> 00:09:47.968
-There you go. -Just so dreamy.

00:09:47.968 --> 00:09:49.467
You're an attractive family. -Okay, well, thank you.

00:09:49.467 --> 00:09:52.033
-Are there other siblings? -No, it's just the two of us.

00:09:52.033 --> 00:09:53.968
[ Laughter ] It's just the two of us.

00:09:53.968 --> 00:09:55.801
I will very happily tell him that.

00:09:55.801 --> 00:09:58.367
And I'm so happy you're here. Congratulations on the show.

00:09:58.367 --> 00:10:02.167
What a delight. Jinkx Monsoon, everybody!

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:06.901
"Chicago" is playing on Broadway at the ambassador Theatre.

00:10:06.901 --> 00:10:09.300
We'll be right back with more "Late Night."

